rgical robot, with timeline adjustments moving your FDA submission to 2026. As someone who specializes in regulatory consulting for the medtech industry, I\'ve helped companies like yours streamline their FDA submissions and reduce delays. NaviSure\'s expertise in de novo submissions could potentially help address some of your integration challenges while preserving capital. Would you be open to a brief discussion about how we\'ve helped similar companies optimize their regulatory strategy during development phases?"\n  },\n  {\n    "name": "Enhao Gong",\n    "company": "Subtle Medical",\n    "title": "CEO & Founder",\n    "rationale": "While Subtle Medical has secured FDA clearances for SubtlePET, SubtleMR, SubtleSYNTH, and SubtleHD, the company likely faces ongoing regulatory challenges with its expanding AI imaging enhancement product portfolio. Their product SubtleGAD, mentioned in 2019, appears to still be in development without announced FDA clearance.",\n    "linkedin_url": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/enhaogong/",\n    "message": "Hi Enhao, congratulations on your recent FDA clearance for SubtleSYNTH. I\'ve been following Subtle Medical\'s progress in AI-powered medical imaging and noticed your expanding product portfolio. As your company continues to innovate with solutions like SubtleGAD, I wanted to connect about NaviSure\'s regulatory consulting services. We specialize in helping AI SaMD companies navigate complex FDA pathways efficiently, often reducing approval timelines by 30%. Would you be interested in discussing how our regulatory expertise might complement your R&D efforts for upcoming submissions?"\n  },\n  {\n    "name": "Elad Walach",\n    "company": "Aidoc",\n    "title": "CEO & Co-founder",\n    "rationale": "While Aidoc has successfully obtained multiple FDA clearances (17 according to their website), the company\'s rapid expansion of AI offerings across different medical imaging applications likely creates ongoing regulatory challenges as they add new capabilities and adapt to evolving FDA guidance for AI/ML-enabled medical devices.",\n    "linkedin_url": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/elad-walach/",\n    "message": "Hi Elad, I\'ve been impressed by Aidoc\'s success in securing 17 FDA clearances for your clinical AI solutions. As the regulatory landscape for AI/ML-enabled devices continues to evolve, I wanted to connect about NaviSure\'s specialized regulatory services. We\'ve helped companies with multi-product AI portfolios streamline their FDA submissions through strategic guidance and deep expertise in the latest AI/ML regulatory frameworks. Given your company\'s continued innovation pace, would you be open to discussing how our approach could help maintain or even accelerate your clearance timeline for upcoming solutions?"\n  },\n  {\n    "name": "Randy Clark",\n    "company": "Vicarious Surgical",\n    "title": "President",\n    "rationale": "Joined Vicarious Surgical as President in early 2024 as the company navigates significant regulatory challenges and timeline delays for their surgical robotics system. The company faces material procurement issues that have further delayed their clinical trials and pushed FDA submission to late 2026.",\n    "linkedin_url": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/randyclark/",\n    "message": "Hi Randy, I noticed you joined Vicarious Surgical as', type='text')]
