nces-FDA-Clearance-of-its-Next-Generation-Handheld-Ultrasound-System-Butterfly-iQ3'), WebSearchResultBlock(encrypted_content='EsUBCioIAxgCIiQ3MjBhMTM3NC0zY2ViLTQ1MDItOGM3MS1jYzcxMzVjOTRmMDgSDHbUELiCQLJZTLWDrhoM+PT8U4xPj12BARW0IjBWl1N+FI4gqesZfhX3aXsSuw7HICK9+L/MANCg4ViiH+/9o2U3q+HTRUyjbziSUCYqSbNledncWkJy08tbnw6SZh7rpLy7L2RXWg2Vc34TzHw37MOELwKzTmachgMn8REui7om+Z1RYJQzj+uEC43n9S+1HXdSmVipn/QYAw==', page_age=None, title='January 4, 2024 Butterfly Network, Inc. Nathan Sabich Senior ...', type='web_search_result', url='https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/cdrh_docs/pdf23/K232808.pdf'), WebSearchResultBlock(encrypted_content='', page_age='April 3, 2023', title='FDA clears AI-enabled lung ultrasound tech from Butterfly Network', type='web_search_result', url='https://www.massdevice.com/fda-clears-ai-lung-ultrasound-butterfly-network/'), WebSearchResultBlock(encrypted_content='', page_age='January 9, 2024', title='FDA clears new point-of-care ultrasound system from Butterfly Network', type='web_search_result', url='https://radiologybusiness.com/topics/medical-imaging/ultrasound-imaging/fda-clears-new-point-care-ultrasound-system-butterfly-network'), WebSearchResultBlock(encrypted_content='', page_age='August 3, 2022', title='Butterfly Network rises on Q2 results, will reduce workforce to extend cash runway', type='web_search_result', url='https://www.massdevice.com/butterfly-network-q2-2022-reduce-workforce/'), WebSearchResultBlock(encrypted_content='', page_age='March 25, 2020', title='Butterfly rescinds features from handheld ultrasound device, working with FDA to re-enable | MobiHealthNews', type='web_search_result', url='https://www.mobihealthnews.com/news/butterfly-rescinds-features-handheld-ultrasound-device-working-fda-re-enable')], tool_use_id='srvtoolu_019KRs9MmJrquBfW1pXURq9Z', type='web_search_tool_result'), TextBlock(citations=None, text='\n\nNow I\'ll compile the information I\'ve gathered into a JSON array of qualified leads:\n\n[\n  {\n    "name": "Elad Walach",\n    "company": "Aidoc",\n    "title": "Co-Founder and CEO",\n    "rationale": "Aidoc has secured 17 FDA clearances (as of 2024) for their AI-powered clinical solutions, but they continue to develop new products that require regulatory approval. The company has been expanding its clinical offerings with new care coordination and patient management solutions for acute medical conditions, indicating ongoing regulatory submissions. Their clearance for a foundation model AI in early 2025 suggests they are navigating complex new regulatory pathways that could benefit from expert guidance.",\n    "linkedin_url": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/elad-walach/",\n    "message": "Hi Elad, I noticed Aidoc\'s impressive track record with 17 FDA clearances and your recent landmark foundation model AI approval. Having worked with several SaMD companies navigating the increasingly complex FDA regulatory landscape, I\'d be interested in discussing how NaviSure might help streamline your future clearance processes, especially as you continue expanding your care coordination solutions for acute conditions. Would you be open to a brief conversation about optimizing your regulatory strategy?"\n  },\n  {\n    "name": "Chris Mansi",\n    "company": "Viz.ai",\n    "title": "Co-Founder and CEO",\n    "rationale": "Viz.ai has secured 13 FDA clearances for their AI algorithms spanning heart, lung, and brain conditions, with their first clearance being a milestone as the first AI-powered diagnostic software to receive FDA clearance for improving patient outcomes in 2018. As the company continues to expand their platform across 1,700 hospitals and health systems, they likely face ongoing regulatory challenges with new algorithms and expanded use cases. Given the recent FDA layoffs in the AI and digital health staff, this could create additional hurdles for their regulatory submissions.",\n    "linkedin_url": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/chris-mansi/",\n    "message": "Hi Chris, congratulations on Viz.ai\'s impressive growth to over 1,700 hospitals and your recognition in the TIME100 AI list. With 13 FDA clearances already secured and likely more in your pipeline, I\'m curious about how the recent FDA staffing changes might be affecting your regulatory timelines. At NaviSure, we\'ve been helping SaMD companies navigate these challenges with specialized expertise. Would you be interested in discussing strategies to maintain your regulatory momentum despite the current FDA constraints?"\n  },\n  {\n    "name": "Joseph DeVivo",\n    "company": "Butterfly Network",\n    "title": "CEO",\n    "rationale": "Butterfly Network has faced specific regulatory challenges, including having to disable two AI-powered software features (Auto Ejection Fraction Tool and Auto Bladder Volume Tool) that were implemented without securing 510(k) clearance. While they received FDA clearance for their next-generation iQ3 device in January 2024 and an AI-enabled auto B-line counter in 2023, their history suggests potential gaps in regulatory strategy. Additionally, the company announced a workforce reduction of approximately 10% in 2022, which may have affected their regulatory affairs staffing.",\n    "linkedin_url": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/joseph-devivo/",\n    "message": "Hi Joseph, I noticed Butterfly Network\'s recent FDA clearances for both the iQ3 device and your AI-enabled auto B-line counter - congratulations! Given your past experience with regulatory challenges around AI features and the workforce adjustments in 2022, I\'m curious if your team has rebuilt its regulatory capacity. At NaviSure, we specialize in helping innovative medical device companies streamline their regulatory pathways, particularly for AI/ML technologies. Would you be open to discussing how we might support your regulatory strategy as you continue to advance your innovative ultrasound solutions?"\n  },\n  {\n    "name": "Randy Hamlin",\n    "company": "Butterfly Network",\n    "title": "Chief Product Officer",\n    "rationale": "As Butterfly Network\'s Chief Product Officer, Randy Hamlin would be directly involved in product development decisions that require regulatory approval. The company\'s history of implementing AI features without proper FDA clearance suggests a potential disconnect between product development and regulatory affairs. With Butterfly', type='text')]
